# Taiga Complete Task Flow (33pol)

All implementation work goes through Taiga. Use MCP server **`user-taiga-mcp`** only. Read schemas under `mcps/user-taiga-mcp/tools/` before each `CallMcpTool`.

**Project:** slug `sadeghhp-33pol` (display **33pol**). User-facing refs: `#8`, `#42`. MCP writes use **internal numeric IDs** (`itemId`, `userStoryId`) from `getMilestone` / `getUserStory` / `advancedSearch`.

Skip Taiga only if the user says so, or for pure Q&A with no project work.

## Flow overview

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A[Session: listProjects + authenticate] --> B[Pick story / sprint]
  B --> C[Story → In progress]
  C --> D{Next open task?}
  D -->|yes| E[Task → In progress]
  E --> F[Implement + dotnet test]
  F --> G[Task → Closed + comment]
  G --> D
  D -->|no| H[Verify all tasks Closed]
  H --> I[Story → Done + comment]
```

## 1. Session start (before any edits)

1. `listProjects` → confirm `sadeghhp-33pol`.
2. `authenticate` if writes may be needed this session.
3. `listMilestones` / `listUserStories` → current sprint and story refs.

**Report to user:** project slug, active story/task ref, current Taiga status.

## 2. Planning (new work)

| Step | Tool |
|------|------|
| Avoid duplicates | `advancedSearch` |
| Epic (multi-sprint) | `createEpic`, `linkStoryToEpic` |
| Story | `createUserStory`, `assignUserStoryToSprint` |
| Decompose | `createTask` / `batchCreateTasks` on `userStoryIdentifier` |
| Sprint | `createMilestone`, `assignUserStoryToSprint` |

Task descriptions: one concern, testable done criteria, ≤ ~half day. Order: models → API → UI.

## 3. Story level

| When | Action |
|------|--------|
| Start implementation on a story | `updateUserStoryStatus` → **In progress** (`userStoryId` = internal id, `projectIdentifier` = slug) |
| All child tasks closed (see §5) | `updateUserStoryStatus` → **Done** + final comment (`dotnet test` summary, closed task refs) |

**Hard gate:** Never mark story **Done** while any task is New / In progress / Needs info. See `taiga-story-done-gate.mdc`.

## 4. Per-task loop (mandatory, one at a time)

At most **one** task **or** issue in an implementation status. Do not start task `#N+1` until `#N` is **Closed** in Taiga (not only in chat).

| Step | When | Action |
|------|------|--------|
| 1 | Before first file edit | Task → **In progress** (REST, see below) |
| 2 | During work | `addComment` on task or story for blockers / meaningful progress |
| 3 | After `dotnet test` passes | Task → **Closed** (REST) + `addComment` (what changed, test excerpt) |
| 4 | Only then | Repeat from step 1 on next task |

```
❌ Code first, Taiga later
❌ Two tasks In progress
❌ Comment "#8 done" while board status is still New

✅ In progress → code → test → Closed + comment → next task
```

### Task status (no MCP `updateTask`)

Close or move tasks via Taiga REST after `authenticate`:

```
PATCH /api/v1/tasks/{id}   body: { "status": <status_id> }
GET   /api/v1/task-statuses?project={projectId}   → resolve In progress / Closed ids
```

Resolve task `id` from `getMilestone` or `advancedSearch` (`type`: `tasks`). If REST fails after one retry: stop, report open refs + manual close list — do not claim done.

## 5. Verify before story Done

1. `getUserStory` or `getMilestone` → list tasks for the story.
2. Confirm **zero** tasks in non-closed status (cancelled/won't-do excepted).
3. `updateUserStoryStatus` → **Done** + comment listing each closed task ref.

**Task-less stories:** Done allowed when acceptance criteria met and verified — no task checklist.

## 6. Bug fixes (issues)

| Step | Tool |
|------|------|
| Create | `createIssue` (repro, expected vs actual, paths) |
| Start fix | `updateIssueStatus` → In progress |
| Done | `updateIssueStatus` → Closed/Done + `addComment` (root cause, tests) |

Same one-active-item rule as tasks.

## 7. MCP failure

1. `authenticate` → retry once.
2. Still failing: tell user which ref failed, paste error, give manual update steps — **do not** claim the step finished.
3. When MCP works again: retro-sync in order (#8 → #9 → …).

## Session end

List every task/issue ref **closed or parked** in Taiga. If story is not Done, name **open task refs** blocking it.
